= The May Thirtieth Movement

Crisis has rocked Shanghai as mass protests erupt, after worker Gu Zhengzhong was shot and killed in May 15th by a Japanese guard hired by his employer.

Because of this, many students began protesting on the streets. Taking a turn for the worse, British guards fired on these protestors on May 30.

This has now turned into open revolt! Because of this, the CPC triggered a general strike and mass protests and the protestors are now calling for the end of the Shanghai International Settlement.

- @next: What happens next?

